wnwards and escape a  situation that an opponent can't follow  you  power items have  the arrived is one of my favorite new  pieces of equipment in halo infinite as  it has not only defensive capabilities  but it can be combined with a bunch of  other actions that makes it extremely  versatile it knocks away enemies and  reflects any projectiles back such as  grenades and rockets and if aimed down  it can act as a nice double jump  one of my favorite ways to use this  though is to pair with your own thrown  grenade if you throw a grenade then use  a repulsor you'll gain a little bit more  reach compared to chucking it normally  even farther if you bank it off a wall  or floor first  and on top of that since frag grenades  only start to explode when they touch  the floor you can throw it down then  repulsor it to roll the grenade and  immediately explode in the enemy's face  instead of the normal delayed explosion  pretty nifty and for lighter vehicles  such as the chopper or the mongoose you  can repulse her and mount the vehicle at  the same time to boost yourself for a  quick escape the timing is pretty tight  though so you may want to practice this  a bit before trying it out live in a  lobby  even though they're relatively weak drop  walls can give the enemy the advantage  of getting a few extra shots in in order  to win the fight but if you're up  against one just shoot the base it  destroys it in one hit  disrupters are probably one of my  favorite new guns when firing at first  it doesn't feel too special but it has a  couple quirks these shots barely do any  damage until the third shot lands which  the enemy then takes slow damage over  time while this damage is pretty  mediocre the moment it starts ticking is  a guaranteed 10 seconds that the enemy  cannot regenerate their shields  while this doesn't seem like a lot of  time in a gunfight 10 seconds is an  eternity and makes this weapon one of  the best support guns in the entire game  paired with good teammates or a strong  secondary weapon makes this really  deadly  both the shock rifle and disrupter have  several extra perks they can both emp  vehicles and disable them and conduct  electricity between players shooting  enemies near each other or any metallic  object like dropped guns or equipment  pads conduct electricity to players and  this can even be paired with a threat  sensor to make a makeshift deployable  shock pole  as the old saying goes  any bladed gun such as a mangler spiker  or shock rifle have just a tad more  melee damage than regular weapons but  this is especially good with the mangler  specifically one shot anywhere plus one  melee doesn't matter the order is all it  takes to kill a spartan  double kill  for any old school halo players lots of  legacy tricks still work today such as  ninja to jump over an enemy and hit them  from behind and combat evolved throwing  grenades at certain weapons to grab them  from a distance which can save you  precious seconds to clutch the match  ah the good old days victory  what was your favorite thing you learned  and if you have any interesting tips or  tricks too share them in the comments  below thanks for watching  [Music]  you
 

